  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation: `node_id` borrows the identity of the source node being checked, with the signature `&self -> &D::NodeId`.\n\n- **Value check:** `labeled_selections_track_only_target_membership_without_reading_contents` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs` builds `ValidationContext::new(&graph, 1)` and asserts `ctx.node_id() == &1`. The context's node (1) differs from the other node queried in the same test (9), so an implementation that returned the wrong node would fail.\n- **Borrow signature:** the call is compared against `&1`, so the return type is a reference. `public_exports_match_the_appendix` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs` checks the public export inventory, not the method signature. The signature is also enforced at compile time.\n- **Gaps:** I found no obligation without a test and no counterexample the assertion would miss. The test marked for `node_id` uses only one node id value. I don't treat that as a gap, because the accessor has no conditional logic and returns a stored field.",
